Package: iphone-mirror-bridge
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: abrham8 <abrham8@users.noreply.github.com>
Depends: python3 (>= 3.9), python3-dbus, python3-gi, gir1.2-glib-2.0, python3-evdev, bluez, uxplay
Recommends: libnotify-bin
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/abrham8/iphone-mirror-bridge
Description: control an iPhone with your Linux touchpad or mouse
 iPhone Mirror Bridge makes a Linux computer act as a Bluetooth mouse for
 an iPhone. With AssistiveTouch enabled on the iPhone, the laptop touchpad
 (or a mouse) moves the iPhone pointer, clicks, scrolls and drags.
 Ctrl+F8 switches the touchpad between the computer and the iPhone.
 .
 The "iPhone Screen Mirroring" app starts an AirPlay receiver (UxPlay) so
 the iPhone screen can be shown on the computer.
